s><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7142169-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7142169</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-7195682-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7195682</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9245511-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9245511</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1041861A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIGUCHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI HIDEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIGUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIGUCHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI HIDEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIGUCHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for manufacturing an electroluminescence device in which a luminescent layer (50) is made to emit light when a desired voltage is applied between an anode (30) and a cathode (60) between which the luminescent layer (50) is interposed, the wavelength of the emitted light is converted to a wavelength of visible light by means of fluorescence conversion films (40A, 40B, 40C) provided for every pixel, comprises forming partition members (20) each having an opening corresponding to a pixel region on a substrate (10), injecting fluorescence conversion precursor (40a, 40b, 40c) into the openings by using a droplet ejecting head (2), and forming fluorescence conversion films (40A, 40B, 40C) by solidifying the fluorescence conversion precursor (40a, 40b, 40c). Thus, the doping ratio of a color conversion component of the fluorescence conversion precursor is suitably adjusted in ejecting the precursor, thereby facilitating the color adjustment of the fluorescence conversion films.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de fabrication d'un dispositif à électroluminescence dans lequel une couche (50) luminescente émet de la lumière lorsqu'une tension désirée est appliquée entre une anode (30) et une cathode (60) entre lesquelles se trouve la couche (50) luminescente. La longueur d'onde de la lumière émise est convertie en une longueur d'onde de lumière visible au moyen de films (40A, 40B, 40C) de conversion de fluorescence prévus pour chaque pixel. Ce procédé consiste à former des éléments (20) de séparation ayant chacun une ouverture correspondant à une région de pixels sur un substrat (10), injecter un précurseur (40a, 40b, 40c) de conversion de fluorescence dans les ouvertures au moyen d'une tête (2) éjectant des gouttelettes et former des films (40A, 40B, 40C) de conversion de fluorescence en solidifiant le précurseur (40a, 40b, 40c). Le rapport de dopage d'un composant de conversion de couleur du précurseur est donc ajusté de manière appropriée lors de l'éjection du précurseur, ce qui facilite le réglage de la couleur des films de conversion de fluorescence.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>